+\subsection*{Prescribing the chromatic cardinal}
+The structural answer does not depend on which uncountable chromatic
+cardinal is prescribed.  The next theorem strengthens the negative
+direction from an avoiding host to a host of any specified uncountable
+chromatic number.
+
+\begin{theoremC}
+Fix a finite integer $r\ge3$ and a finite simple $r$-uniform
+hypergraph $F$.  If $F\notin\mathcal B_r$, then for every uncountable
+cardinal $\kappa$ there is an $F$-free $r$-uniform hypergraph $H$
+with $\chi(H)=\kappa$.  If $F$ is linear, one may also require
+$|V(H)|\le2^{<\kappa}$.  If $F\in\mathcal B_r$, no such host exists.
+\end{theoremC}
+
+Here $2^{<\kappa}=\sup_{\nu<\kappa}2^\nu$, with the supremum
+taken over cardinals.  Theorem~\ref{exact-avoidance-spectrum} proves
+the assertion, including singular $\kappa$.
+Li established the triple-system spectrum \citep[Theorem~7.1]{li2026}.
+For linear forbidden systems in higher uniformity, the key identity is
+$\chi(\mathcal L_\kappa(H))=\min\{\chi(H),\kappa\}$ for the
+sequence lift of height $\kappa$.  It combines exact chromatic control
+with the finite trace theorem already used for the classification.
+
+Nonlinear forbidden systems require a different construction.
+We extend Li's reservoir method \citep[Section~6]{li2026} to add several
+old vertices to a labelled base edge.  With the simultaneous-colour
+systems of Erd\H{o}s--Galvin--Hajnal \citep[Corollary~12.3]{egh1975},
+this gives, for $1\le i\le r-2$, an $r$-uniform host with pairwise
+edge intersections at most $i$, chromatic number exactly $\mu^+$,
+and order at most $\beth_{\lceil(r-1)/i\rceil}(\mu)$.
+Here $\beth_0(\mu)=\mu$ and $\beth_{j+1}(\mu)=2^{\beth_j(\mu)}$.
+The order bounds are in ZFC; the corresponding optimal GCH thresholds
+are classical consequences of Erd\H{o}s--Galvin--Hajnal.
+
+The same lift avoids any finite family of linear non-obligatory systems
+simultaneously.  This family theorem has a real boundary: for every
+uniformity there is a finite mixed family whose members are individually
+avoidable at every uncountable cardinal, while their simultaneous
+omission forces countable chromatic number
+(Proposition~\ref{exact-mixed-family-obstruction}).
+The new results in Sections~\ref{uniform-extension}
+and~\ref{exact-spectra-extension} have manuscript proofs; they are
+not additional Lean-verified endpoints.
 
